e. Sorry, Bear, but this is the current reality. Your work is very appreciated. A very fine image, obviously deserving a much higher score as it would have happened when we had 100+ votes in each challenge and few low votes wouldn''t make much difference. PS My membership expires in a few days, I may let it lapse and maybe come for one month when I get motivated.  Exactly my mind. This site doesn''t please me anymore. And I don''t know the solution to it', '2018-05-14 06:11:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7568419, 1214536, 147314, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Sisto:</b></div><hr/><i> totally agree with marnet; this is a masterpiece and when gyaban plays the second place is a first one for we commons mortals </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The fact <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=114969" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Gyaban </a> has an entry doesn''t automatically means he should win. I do love his creations and would like to have the ability to achieve something that''s only 10% of the quality he delivers. But in this specific challenge I think the Blue Ribbon is well deserved by Art, it really meets the challenge and is well executed.<br/>But the low numbers of participants is becoming more and more an issue and the same with the low number of votes. And I''m sure that a couple of people that vote is voting low just because they can or maybe to benefit their own entry. Maybe there should be a commitment to write a comment when you give 1-3 and also when you give 8-10 (works both ways), but we all know that''s not going to happen, causing more and more people to turn their back to the site :-(<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-05-14 17:33:16.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Sisto: totally agree with marnet; this is a masterpiece and when gyaban plays the second place is a first one for we commons mortals  The fact  Gyaban  has an entry doesn''t automatically means he should win. I do love his creations and would like to have the ability to achieve something that''s only 10% of the quality he delivers. But in this specific challenge I think the Blue Ribbon is well deserved by Art, it really meets the challenge and is well executed.But the low numbers of participants is becoming more and more an issue and the same with the low number of votes. And I''m sure that a couple of people that vote is voting low just because they can or maybe to benefit their own entry. Maybe there should be a commitment to write a comment when you give 1-3 and also when you give 8-10 (works both ways), but we all know that''s not going to happen, causing more and more people to turn their back to the site :-(', '2018-05-14 06:33:46.000000', '2018-05-14 18:33:16.000000', 0),
(7568420, 1214544, 123833, '<td valign="top">Very nice effort, Ken. I did not mean to lessen the appreciation of your work by my comment on Christophe''s entry. It is a great thing you did for the memory of Greg.  I did not know him but I see that he is a fellow Aussie.</td>', 'Very nice effort, Ken. I did not mean to lessen the appreciation of your work by my comment on Christophe''s entry. It is a great thing you did for the memory of Greg.  I did not know him but I see that he is a fellow Aussie.', '2018-05-14 06:35:54.000000', NULL, 0),
