(7568428, 1214536, 60581, '<td valign="top">Welcome back!!!!! what a piece of work!</td>', 'Welcome back!!!!! what a piece of work!', '2018-05-14 12:14:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7568430, 1214541, 109363, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> My favorite of the challenge. Great shapes, great colors, great expression. I wouldn''t mind a tutorial, very curious about your technique! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>wow, that comment coming from you is quite an honor, as well as humbling.<br/> <br/>the starter image was my face behind a block of glass, using an outtake from this entry a few years ago<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1093170" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1841/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1093170.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1841/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1093170.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1841/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1093170.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>i then just used Deep Dream Generator, an online photo editor that grew out of the artificial/computer vision field, <br/> <br/><a href="https://deepdreamgenerator.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Deep Dream Generator</a> <br/> <br/>and using on of their "seed" textures until i got the result i wanted.<br/> <br/>then i blended back the original image to get my eye back, and did a few other adjustments to strcuture, contrast, etc.<br/> <br/>its a really fun process, and you can waste hours just experimenting</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: My favorite of the challenge. Great shapes, great colors, great expression. I wouldn''t mind a tutorial, very curious about your technique!   wow, that comment coming from you is quite an honor, as well as humbling. the starter image was my face behind a block of glass, using an outtake from this entry a few years ago   i then just used Deep Dream Generator, an online photo editor that grew out of the artificial/computer vision field,  Deep Dream Generator  and using on of their "seed" textures until i got the result i wanted. then i blended back the original image to get my eye back, and did a few other adjustments to strcuture, contrast, etc. its a really fun process, and you can waste hours just experimenting', '2018-05-14 12:17:49.000000', NULL, 0),
